ROUND-3 RE-REVIEW — 4 LOW, on f82f9e88
================================================================

L1 a transfer rule is not RECORDED as a transfer — NAMED, NOT FIXED.
   The reviewer's own recommendation ("Fix: none here — worth its own finding").
   `bank_categorisation_rules` has no transfer column, so the sweep writes
   source 'auto_bank_recon' / allocation_type 'account' with no
   counterparty_account_id, no transfer_journal_entry_id and no
   duplicate-transfer guard. Amounts are right, shape is not. Giving rules a
   transfer shape is a schema change and its own work, not part of a VAT
   correction — doing it inside this commit would be the wrong call. Written
   up in K-017 fix.md and in the bank/.claude.md recent-changes entry so it
   cannot be lost.
L2 the batched caller converted "absent" into "not a bank" — FIXED.
   bankRulesMatchingService now passes `ruleAccountIsBank.get(id)` unchanged.
   NO TEST ASSERTS THIS, deliberately: the map is built from the same id list,
   so an id can only be absent when the account does not exist for the company,
   and the journal insert then fails on the FK first. It is a contract
   alignment with no reachable behaviour change, and a test would prove
   nothing. The contract it aligns TO is reachable at the MCP prefetch and is
   tested there — 'falls back when only the bank fact is missing from the
   prefetch' in allocationVatGuardBatch.test.ts.
L3 BankRuleForm still offered a treatment for a TRANSFER rule — FIXED.
   `accountSubtype` now flows from the chart of accounts through
   useBankRuleRefData into GLAccountOption, and `postsNoVat` covers the bank
   contra as well as the two settlement shapes. Wording differs per case, and
   a rule that is both a settlement and a bank contra says settlement, because
   a supplier rule ignores its GL account entirely.
L4 the bank-contra guard had no real-database test — FIXED.
   New case in k016-k017-settlement-vat-adjacent.int.test.ts drives the real
   `applyRules` over a rule pointing at a second gl_accounts row with
   account_subtype = 'bank': one entry, two lines, R345 gross on the
   counterparty bank, vat_input untouched, journal balanced.

